# Generated files: GitHub collapses them in diffs so a review starts from the
# code. They are checked by tools, not by reading: the sqlx query metadata by
# the SQLX_OFFLINE build in CI (`make db-prepare` writes it), the lockfiles by
# --locked / --frozen-lockfile and the acceptance verifier's supply-chain
# check. The API types are regenerated with `make api-generate`; NOTE: CI does
# not yet regenerate and compare them, so a stale schema.gen.ts is caught only
# indirectly by typecheck and tests. New packages a lockfile brings in are
# listed in the PR description instead.
backend/.sqlx/** linguist-generated=true
frontend/src/api/schema.gen.ts linguist-generated=true
backend/Cargo.lock linguist-generated=true
frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true
